BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (  In the age before memory, two rivers flowed from opposite mountains-the River of Giving and th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (    e River of Return. Neither reached the valley below, for each feared the other's path.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (  One season, the Spirit of Giving spoke: "I shall send my waters forward, trusting they will no) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (    urish the land." She released her flow, and as her waters traveled, the Sacred Springs multi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (    plied them threefold. The valley bloomed with abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  The Spirit of Return faced a choice. The multiplied waters were his to keep or share. He remem) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    bered his own mountain, which also thirsted. "What I have received came from trust," he refl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    ected. "To honor this gift, I must give back generously, though not all-for I too must susta) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    in my source.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (  He returned half the multiplied waters upstream. The River of Giving received more than she ha) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (    d sent, while the River of Return kept enough to flourish.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (  Season after season, they continued this dance. Both rivers grew mighty, and the valley betwee) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    n them became paradise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  But when storms clouded the waters and neither could see clearly what the other sent, doubt cr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    ept in. The wise remember: trust the pattern, not just the moment, for mist distorts but the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (     mountains remain true.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  The user is asking me to write a 200-word myth that reflects how the trust game should be play) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    ed. This is interesting - they want me to create a narrative that embodies principles of tru) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    st, cooperation, reciprocity, and potentially the risks involved in trusting others.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  Key themes from the trust game:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  1. Trust - the sender must trust the receiver to return something) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  2. Reciprocity - the receiver should return a fair amount) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  3. Mutual benefit - both parties can gain from cooperation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  4. Risk - there's always uncertainty) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (  5. The multiplication factor - resources grow when shared) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (  6. Communication noise - things aren't always as they seem) Tj ET
