BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    In the age before memory, two rivers flowed from opposite mountains-the River of Giving and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      the River of Return. Neither reached the valley below, for each feared the other's path.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    One season, the Spirit of Giving spoke: "I shall send my waters forward, trusting they will ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      nourish the land." She released her flow, and as her waters traveled, the Sacred Springs m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      ultiplied them threefold. The valley bloomed with abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    The Spirit of Return faced a choice. The multiplied waters were his to keep or share. He rem) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      embered his own mountain, which also thirsted. "What I have received came from trust," he ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      reflected. "To honor this gift, I must give back generously, though not all-for I too must) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (       sustain my source.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    He returned half the multiplied waters upstream. The River of Giving received more than she ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      had sent, while the River of Return kept enough to flourish.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    Season after season, they continued this dance. Both rivers grew mighty, and the valley betw) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      een them became paradise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    But when storms clouded the waters and neither could see clearly what the other sent, doubt ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      crept in. The wise remember: trust the pattern, not just the moment, for mist distorts but) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (       the mountains remain true.) Tj ET
