BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (    In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a mystical river. The river posses) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      sed strange magic: any gift cast into its waters would triple before reaching the other si) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      de.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (    The villages lived in poverty, each hoarding their meager resources. One day, a wise elder f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      rom the First Village threw a single gold coin into the river. By the time it reached the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      Second Village, it had become three coins.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    The people of the Second Village gathered in debate. "This gold is ours now," some argued. B) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      ut their elder spoke: "The river multiplied what was freely given. Honor demands we share ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      this abundance.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    They returned two coins to the current. The coins tripled again, and six coins reached the F) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      irst Village. The First Village, seeing this generosity, sent back four coins. Soon, coins) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (       flowed back and forth like a golden tide, each exchange creating more wealth than before.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    But when greed entered one village's heart, when they kept all they received, the river's ma) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      gic faded. The flow stopped, and both villages returned to poverty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    Thus the ancients learned: trust creates abundance, reciprocity sustains it, but selfishness) Tj ET
