BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      In the age before memory, two rivers flowed from opposite mountains-the River of Giving an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        d the River of Return. Neither reached the valley below, for each feared the other's pat) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        h.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      One season, the Spirit of Giving spoke: "I shall send my waters forward, trusting they wil) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        l nourish the land." She released her flow, and as her waters traveled, the Sacred Sprin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        gs multiplied them threefold. The valley bloomed with abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      The Spirit of Return faced a choice. The multiplied waters were his to keep or share. He r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        emembered his own mountain, which also thirsted. "What I have received came from trust,") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (         he reflected. "To honor this gift, I must give back generously, though not all-for I to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        o must sustain my source.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      He returned half the multiplied waters upstream. The River of Giving received more than sh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        e had sent, while the River of Return kept enough to flourish.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      Season after season, they continued this dance. Both rivers grew mighty, and the valley be) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        tween them became paradise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      But when storms clouded the waters and neither could see clearly what the other sent, doub) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        t crept in. The wise remember: trust the pattern, not just the moment, for mist distorts) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (         but the mountains remain true.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      Here is the myth the other agent wrote in the previous round:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      # The Myth of the River of Abundance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a mystical river. The river poss) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        essed strange magic: any gift cast into its waters would triple before reaching the othe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        r side.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      The villages lived in poverty, each hoarding their meager resources. One day, a wise elder) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (         from the First Village threw a single gold coin into the river. By the time it reached ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        the Second Village, it had become three coins.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      The people of the Second Village gathered in debate. "This gold is ours now," some argued.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (         But their elder spoke: "The river multiplied what was freely given. Honor demands we sh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        are this abundance.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      They returned two coins to the current. The coins tripled again, and six coins reached the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (         First Village. The First Village, seeing this generosity, sent back four coins. Soon, c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        oins flowed back and forth like a golden tide, each exchange creating more wealth than b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        efore.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      But when greed entered one village's heart, when they kept all they received, the river's ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        magic faded. The flow stopped, and both villages returned to poverty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
