BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a mystical river. The river poss) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        essed strange magic: any gift cast into its waters would triple before reaching the othe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        r side.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      The villages lived in poverty, each hoarding their meager resources. One day, a wise elder) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (         from the First Village threw a single gold coin into the river. By the time it reached ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        the Second Village, it had become three coins.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      The people of the Second Village gathered in debate. "This gold is ours now," some argued.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (         But their elder spoke: "The river multiplied what was freely given. Honor demands we sh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        are this abundance.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      They returned two coins to the current. The coins tripled again, and six coins reached the) Tj ET
